<p>Finding a 2-bedroom apartment in Lewisville, TX comes down to picking the right part of town first, then the right community. Lewisville has a walkable Old Town, a newer upscale corridor along SH 121 and Castle Hills, and quieter pockets near Lewisville Lake. Below are communities worth touring, who each one tends to suit and what to confirm before you sign.</p>

<h2>How to Think About Lewisville Neighborhoods</h2>
<p>Lewisville sits in the Dallas-Fort Worth area between Dallas and Denton, with I-35E and SH 121 doing most of the commuting work. Broadly, you will see three kinds of options:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Old Town:</strong> walkable streets, local restaurants and community events.</li>
<li><strong>Castle Hills and the SH 121 corridor:</strong> newer, amenity-heavy communities close to shopping and big employers along 121.</li>
<li><strong>West and southwest Lewisville:</strong> established neighborhoods, often with more modest pricing and quick access to the lake.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Lewisville Communities to Tour for a 2-Bedroom</h2>
<p>These communities were highlighted for 2-bedroom living. Rents, floor plans and amenities change often, so use each link to check current pricing and availability.</p>

<h3>1. Main and Mill</h3>
<p><a href="https://oldtownlewisville.com/listing/main-mill-lofts-pre-leasing/">Main and Mill</a> is in Old Town Lewisville, which makes it a natural fit if you want to walk to dinner, coffee and local events. It suits renters who care more about neighborhood character than a big suburban amenity package.</p>

<h3>2. Toscana at Valley Ridge</h3>
<p><a href="https://www.toscanaatvalleyridgeapts.com/">Toscana at Valley Ridge</a> is on the west side of Lewisville off Valley Ridge Boulevard. It tends to appeal to renters who want a resort-style community feel with reasonable access to I-35E and the lake area.</p>

<h3>3. Olivian at The Realm</h3>
<p><a href="https://riseapartments.com/apartment/olivian-at-the-realm/">Olivian at The Realm</a> is part of The Realm development along SH 121. It is a good one to look at if you work along the 121 corridor or want quick access to shopping and dining in the area.</p>

<h3>4. Cortland at Castle Hills</h3>
<p><a href="https://cortland.com/apartments/cortland-at-castle-hills/">Cortland at Castle Hills</a> sits in the Castle Hills area off SH 121. Pet owners and commuters often shortlist communities here; ask the leasing team about current pet policies and any smart-home features in the unit you would lease.</p>

<h3>5. Tapestry at The Realm</h3>
<p><a href="https://www.apartments.com/tapestry-at-the-realm-lewisville-tx/xcwts8n/">Tapestry at The Realm</a> is another community in The Realm at Castle Hills. It suits renters looking for a newer, upscale building in a planned, walkable-feeling district.</p>

